{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And He spoke.</b> Behold, the children of Israel, who are Your people, did not listen to me, so how will Pharaoh listen to me—he being a king and not of Your people? Moreover, it is a great deficiency that I should speak before him while I am uncircumcised of lips, for the first time You promised me that You would put the words in my mouth so that I would not stammer at the letter that is difficult for me. Perhaps my tongue will stumble before him, and You said that Aaron would be an interpreter between me and Israel:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:08.342161188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}